Negative control for the row error's NO-FILL law (H8 · AC6.2).

Puts the danger wash back on the refused row and the refused card — the
treatment the ruling killed. The ring is left exactly where it is, so what this
plants is only the fill: the errored row's computed background stops equalling a
normal row's, and the record is marked by a colour over its surface rather than
by the ui's own invalid outline around it.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the row-ring spec — the errored row's background equals a normal row's,
and the card carries the identical treatment (H8 in card view).

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.styles.ts b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.styles.ts
